SensorLoop draws a spec block of control points or signals where each one sits on one storage and distribution loop: a flat P&ID on a navy sheet, an instrument balloon with its real tag letters over the row number on every measuring point, hoses numbered at their ends, and the rows as keyed notes along the foot.

- Look `sensor-loop` (`assets/src/blocks/look-sensor-loop.js`) on a `spec` block. Live on ind-personal-care "Where microbes get in, and what the package does"; specimen content from sys-monitoring "Sensors and signals" (retired there) still renders. Pass 12 rebuild after concept 202 (`design-system/inspiration/gemini/202-p12-ind-personal-care-microbes.png`): the pass 9 IsoKit drawing (which drew a TOC analyser and a divert valve no personal-care row states, with 10 px balloons) is replaced; the concept's "ISA" balloon text and garbled notes are not used.
- The loop: tank, supply run with the circulation pump, then only the measuring points the rows name, in water order (UV, TOC, conductivity, temperature, divert valve with its drain), then the points of use hanging off the supply (two sample tees first when a row names sample ports), and the return run back to the tank top with the flow element. Data recording (desktop) is a recorder inside the loop with a dashed signal line from each balloon.
- Tags: FIT flow, CIT conductivity, AIT TOC, TIT temperature, XV divert valve, SP sample point, UV the UV unit; points of use carry the hoses row's number. A further point of the same row (second sample tee) has a dashed balloon.
- Markup: `div.aq-sensor-loop` (navy sheet) → `div.__fig` (`svg.__svg--d` horizontal, `svg.__svg--p` vertical; inside: `__wall`/`__bore` twin-wall pipe, `__tank`, `g.__mk[data-sl]` symbols, `__stem`, `g.__ball[data-sl]` with `__tg` and `__nu`, `__ht` hose numbers, `__bus`) and `ol.__cards` of `li.__card[data-sl]` (`p.__n` number and `__ntag`, `h3.__p`, `p.__v`, `p.__m`). `p.__note` after.
- Fields: `h`, `caption` (eyebrow), `intro`, `rows [{p, v, m, site}]`, `note`, `fold`, `fold_noun` (phones only). `site`: `flow | uv | cond | toc | temp | divert | data`; a row without one is placed by its words ("sample" → sample tees; "hose", "point of use", "outlet" → the hoses) or is a note only.
- Pointing at a note (or a mark) lights its balloons, stems and symbols (`flow` fill, `limestone` lines).
- Text: balloon and hose labels 13 px mono at 1:1 on desktop, 13.5 px in a 340-unit phone drawing (12.4 px rendered); notes 17/24 titles, 15/22 values, 14/20 notes.
- **Phones** (≤ 860 px): the loop recomposed vertically: the tank at the top, the supply a riser with the balloons to its left and the branches and hoses to its right, the return up the left edge with its FIT balloon; then every note in one column. About 1,900 px with six rows (the old phone drawing was 120 px tall with 5 px labels).

## Motion

On scroll-in the pipe walls draw round the loop (DrawSVG 1.2 s), the equipment fades up, each balloon strikes on in water order as its stem drops, and the notes print along the foot. Once, under 3 s; nothing under reduced motion.
